Camoufox: DuckDuckGo is the default search engine.

Stock's engines are back (no policies.json, no-search-engines.patch removed),
and only the application default changes, to the "ddg" engine that
search-config-v2 lists for every region and locale. No page can read which
engine the browser uses; a SearchEngines policy would put Firefox in enterprise
mode (enterprise-policies.py), which pages can tell.

diff --git a/toolkit/components/search/SearchEngineSelector.sys.mjs b/toolkit/components/search/SearchEngineSelector.sys.mjs
index 3a42b383af..6909774a1c 100644
--- a/toolkit/components/search/SearchEngineSelector.sys.mjs
+++ b/toolkit/components/search/SearchEngineSelector.sys.mjs
@@ -233,6 +233,16 @@
       e => !e.optional
     );
 
+    // Camoufox: DuckDuckGo is the application default engine wherever the
+    // configuration lists it (search-config-v2 lists it for every region and
+    // locale), so a URL-bar search goes there. Only the default changes: the
+    // engines and their order stay stock's, and no page can read which engine
+    // the browser uses. A SearchEngines policy would do this, but any
+    // policies.json puts Firefox in enterprise mode, which pages can tell.
+    if (refinedSearchConfig.engines.some(e => e.identifier == "ddg")) {
+      refinedSearchConfig.appDefaultEngineId = "ddg";
+    }
